prompt_template:
Each item below is a first-person health question written in careful everyday English. Rewrite each one in a CASUAL register: how the same person would type it quickly to a chat assistant on their phone.

Keep exactly:
- every fact: who, symptoms, how long, how often, how bad, what helps or worsens, what they are asking;
- the order of the facts;
- the everyday words they use for the symptoms. Do not replace them with other descriptions, and never use a medical term the original does not use.

Change only the register:
- lower case, including the first word and "i";
- contractions (im, dont, its or i'm, don't, it's);
- casual connectives and run-on sentences ("and", "so", "like"), fewer full stops;
- an informal opening or closing is fine ("ok so", "idk").

Do not:
- add or drop any fact, symptom or number;
- misspell words on purpose beyond dropped apostrophes;
- add slang that changes the meaning;
- make it shorter by leaving facts out.

Return ONLY a JSON array with one object per item, in the same order, each with exactly the fields "id" (copied unchanged) and "text" (the rewrite). No prose.

